    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d492">

                <pb facs="0890" n="780" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg780"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr. Scruggs.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-05-19"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 19,
                        1890</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 85.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose, for your information and the
                    files of your legation, copy of Mr. Lincoln’s No. 229<anchor n="*"
                        xml:id="d492-f1"/> of the 5th instant, reporting his conversation with Lord
                    Salisbury in regard to the renewal of diplomatic relations between Great Britain
                    and Venezuela and the settlement of the boundary dispute by arbitration.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James G. Blaine.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d492-f1" n="*" xml:id="d492-f1-content">
                <p>See correspondence with the legation of the United States at London.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
